$DIR/main.p:4:22: cannot return (*N)(new(N)), which points into the temporary owned[N] that new(N) returns
    (*N)(new(N)) points into the temporary owned[N] that new(N) returns. The
    owned[N] made at main.p:4 is a temporary: nothing keeps it, so its object is
    dropped at the end of the statement. A view of the object may be passed to
    calls in that statement but may not outlive it. At the end of the statement,
    the temporary is dropped, before the caller gets (*N)(new(N)), so it would
    point at a value that has been dropped.
    The view does not own the memory it looks at. Nothing keeps the temporary
    after the statement, so a stored view would outlive the value that keeps its
    memory alive.
    Return the owned[N] itself, which keeps its memory alive in the caller, or a
    copy of what the view looks at.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3009" for a longer explanation)
